"""RUN-05 data: the requirements of every level below the device, in the order Sanad's allocator numbers them.
Read by tools/pinned-build.py. Each row:
  id (the id the allocator is expected to give; the build refuses if it gives another), parents (ids of the PARENT
  node only), title, statement, rationale, verification,
  impl = [(C file under 10-src/firmware/components, line of an existing @implements marker)],
  ver  = [(test file under 10-src, test function)] or ["SP-nn"] (system procedure rows).
MAP turns run 2's subsystem / hardware-leaf ids (which do not exist in this run) into this run's ids, for the
code markers and the system procedure rows. DRAFT — needs Masood's review."""

